{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He made him ride on the high places of the earth.</b> This He will do because He did not attain His purpose in the giving of Torah mentioned above, and He seeks this a second time by giving them the land, as it says: למען אשר ישמרו חקיו — 'in order that they keep His statutes' (Psalms 105:45) — to bring them to perfection by causing them to ride upon an elevated portion of the earth in place and in rank, as it says: צבי היא לכל הארצות — 'it is the beauty of all lands' (Ezekiel 20:6). This will be upon their entry into the land now." "<b>And he ate the produce of the field.</b> That they did not toil for them, as it says: כרמים וזיתים אשר לא נטעתם אתם אכלים — 'vineyards and olive trees that you did not plant, you eat' (Joshua 24:13)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:01.443890212Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}